    <section class="learning-section sorting-home-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
                <span class="section-kicker">SORTING · 01–07</span>
                <h2>Compare strategies, not just final arrays.</h2>
            </div>
            <p>Every sorting lab uses the same Build → Predict → Watch → Explain → Practice rhythm, while Visual and Memory State expose the behavior unique to that algorithm.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="path-grid module-grid">
            <a class="path-card available module-card" href="/sorting/bubble">
                <div class="card-topline"><span class="path-index">01 · BEGINNER</span><span class="status-pill live"><i></i> Ready</span></div>
                <div class="path-icon sort-icon"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <h3>Bubble Sort</h3><p>Adjacent comparisons, swaps, sorted suffix and adaptive early exit.</p>
                <div class="concept-row"><span>Stable</span><span>Θ(n²)</span><span>Early exit</span></div><span class="card-link">Open lesson <b>→</b></span>
            </a>
            <a class="path-card available module-card" href="/sorting/selection">
                <div class="card-topline"><span class="path-index">02 · BEGINNER</span><span class="status-pill live"><i></i> Ready</span></div>
                <div class="path-icon sort-icon"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <h3>Selection Sort</h3><p>Separate minimum search from the one distant swap that finishes each prefix position.</p>
                <div class="concept-row"><span>Minimum</span><span>Few swaps</span><span>Unstable</span></div><span class="card-link">Open lesson <b>→</b></span>
            </a>
            <a class="path-card available module-card" href="/sorting/insertion">
                <div class="card-topline"><span class="path-index">03 · BEGINNER</span><span class="status-pill live"><i></i> Ready</span></div>
                <div class="path-icon sort-icon"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <h3>Insertion Sort</h3><p>Grow a sorted prefix by shifting a contiguous block and inserting one key.</p>
                <div class="concept-row"><span>Adaptive</span><span>Stable</span><span>Online</span></div><span class="card-link">Open lesson <b>→</b></span>
            </a>
            <a class="path-card available module-card" href="/sorting/merge">
                <div class="card-topline"><span class="path-index">04 · INTERMEDIATE</span><span class="status-pill live"><i></i> Ready</span></div>
                <div class="path-icon sort-icon"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <h3>Merge Sort</h3><p>Split into runs, merge with a reusable buffer, and compare top-down with natural runs.</p>
                <div class="concept-row"><span>Stable</span><span>Θ(n log n)</span><span>O(n) buffer</span></div><span class="card-link">Open lesson <b>→</b></span>
            </a>
            <a class="path-card available module-card" href="/sorting/quick">
                <div class="card-topline"><span class="path-index">05 · INTERMEDIATE</span><span class="status-pill live"><i></i> Ready</span></div>
                <div class="path-icon sort-icon"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <h3>Quick Sort</h3><p>Choose a pivot, partition the active range and see how recursion shape controls cost.</p>
                <div class="concept-row"><span>Pivot</span><span>Partition</span><span>3-way</span></div><span class="card-link">Open lesson <b>→</b></span>
            </a>
            <a class="path-card available module-card" href="/sorting/heap">
                <div class="card-topline"><span class="path-index">06 · ADVANCED</span><span class="status-pill live advanced"><i></i> Ready</span></div>
                <div class="path-icon sort-icon"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <h3>Heap Sort</h3><p>Build a Max Heap in the same array, extract the root and grow a final sorted suffix.</p>
                <div class="concept-row"><span>Floyd</span><span>Θ(n log n)</span><span>O(1) extra</span></div><span class="card-link">Open lesson <b>→</b></span>
            </a>
            <a class="path-card available module-card" href="/graph-algorithms/topological">
                <div class="card-topline"><span class="path-index">07 · ADVANCED</span><span class="status-pill live advanced"><i></i> Ready</span></div>
                <div class="path-icon graph-icon"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <h3>Topological Sort</h3><p>Order directed dependencies with Kahn's Queue or DFS reverse postorder, and reject cycles that make a valid ordering impossible.</p>
                <div class="concept-row"><span>DAG</span><span>Indegree</span><span>O(V + E)</span></div><span class="card-link">Open lesson <b>→</b></span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="learning-section search-home-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
                <span class="section-kicker">SEARCH &amp; TRAVERSAL · 01–06</span>
                <h2>Find values by following the evidence.</h2>
            </div>
            <p>Start with value search, move through graph traversal, then finish with advanced weighted search and minimum-connectivity problems.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="path-grid module-grid">
            <a class="path-card available module-card" href="/search/linear">
                <div class="card-topline"><span class="path-index">01 · BEGINNER</span><span class="status-pill live"><i></i> Ready</span></div>
                <div class="path-icon sort-icon"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <h3>Linear Search</h3><p>Scan index 0 → n−1, stop at the first match, and connect the visited prefix directly to Θ(1) and Θ(n).</p>
                <div class="concept-row"><span>First match</span><span>Θ(n)</span><span>Read-only</span></div><span class="card-link">Open lesson <b>→</b></span>
            </a>
            <a class="path-card available module-card" href="/search/binary">
                <div class="card-topline"><span class="path-index">02 · BEGINNER</span><span class="status-pill live"><i></i> Ready</span></div>
                <div class="path-icon sort-icon"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <h3>Binary Search</h3><p>Shrink a sorted candidate range with left/right/mid, then compare any-match with first-occurrence duplicate handling.</p>
                <div class="concept-row"><span>Sorted input</span><span>Θ(log n)</span><span>First occurrence</span></div><span class="card-link">Open lesson <b>→</b></span>
            </a>
            <a class="path-card available module-card" href="/search/bfs">
                <div class="card-topline"><span class="path-index">03 · INTERMEDIATE</span><span class="status-pill live"><i></i> Ready</span></div>
                <div class="path-icon graph-icon"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <h3>Breadth-First Search</h3><p>Use a manual FIFO Queue to expand the reachable graph layer by layer and build unweighted shortest-path distances.</p>
                <div class="concept-row"><span>Queue</span><span>Levels</span><span>O(V + E)</span></div><span class="card-link">Open lesson <b>→</b></span>
            </a>
            <a class="path-card available module-card" href="/search/dfs">
                <div class="card-topline"><span class="path-index">04 · INTERMEDIATE</span><span class="status-pill live"><i></i> Ready</span></div>
                <div class="path-icon graph-icon"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <h3>Depth-First Search</h3><p>Compare recursive call-stack DFS with an explicit manual Stack and watch backtracking through one branch at a time.</p>
                <div class="concept-row"><span>Stack</span><span>Backtrack</span><span>O(V + E)</span></div><span class="card-link">Open lesson <b>→</b></span>
            </a>
            <a class="path-card available module-card" href="/graph-algorithms/dijkstra">
                <div class="card-topline"><span class="path-index">05 · ADVANCED</span><span class="status-pill live advanced"><i></i> Ready</span></div>
                <div class="path-icon graph-icon"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <h3>Dijkstra</h3><p>Search a weighted graph for shortest paths by relaxing non-negative edges and always expanding the best current distance.</p>
                <div class="concept-row"><span>Relaxation</span><span>Shortest path</span><span>Min-heap</span></div><span class="card-link">Open lesson <b>→</b></span>
            </a>
            <a class="path-card available module-card" href="/graph-algorithms/mst">
                <div class="card-topline"><span class="path-index">06 · ADVANCED</span><span class="status-pill live advanced"><i></i> Ready</span></div>
                <div class="path-icon graph-icon"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <h3>Minimum Spanning Tree</h3><p>Find the cheapest set of edges that keeps the graph connected, then compare Prim with Kruskal and Union-Find.</p>
                <div class="concept-row"><span>Prim</span><span>Kruskal</span><span>Union-Find</span></div><span class="card-link">Open lesson <b>→</b></span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>


    <section class="learning-section ai-home-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
                <span class="section-kicker">MACHINE LEARNING · PHASE 1 · 02–06</span>
                <h2>Optimize first, train simple models, then reason from nearby examples.</h2>
            </div>
            <p>Vector now lives with Data Structures. The ML track starts with optimization, trains two regression models, then switches to local neighbor-based classification with KNN before introducing KD-Tree acceleration.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="path-grid module-grid">
            <a class="path-card available module-card" href="/ml-foundations/gradient-descent">
                <div class="card-topline"><span class="path-index">02 · OPTIMIZATION</span><span class="status-pill live"><i></i> Ready</span></div>
                <div class="path-icon sort-icon"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <h3>Gradient Descent</h3><p>Follow one simple loop: measure the slope, take a controlled step downhill, and repeat until the slope is small.</p>
                <div class="concept-row"><span>Slope</span><span>Step size</span><span>Stop rule</span></div><span class="card-link">Open lesson <b>→</b></span>
            </a>
            <a class="path-card available module-card" href="/ml-foundations/linear-regression">
                <div class="card-topline"><span class="path-index">03 · MODEL</span><span class="status-pill live"><i></i> Ready</span></div>
                <div class="path-icon sort-icon"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <h3>Linear Regression</h3><p>Fit a line to examples, inspect residuals and MSE, and train weight + bias with Gradient Descent.</p>
                <div class="concept-row"><span>Prediction</span><span>Residual</span><span>MSE</span></div><span class="card-link">Open lesson <b>→</b></span>
            </a>
            <a class="path-card available module-card" href="/ml-foundations/logistic-regression">
                <div class="card-topline"><span class="path-index">04 · CLASSIFICATION</span><span class="status-pill live"><i></i> Ready</span></div>
                <div class="path-icon sort-icon"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <h3>Logistic Regression</h3><p>Keep the weighted score, add sigmoid probability, and learn a binary decision boundary.</p>
                <div class="concept-row"><span>Sigmoid</span><span>Probability</span><span>Boundary</span></div><span class="card-link">Open lesson <b>→</b></span>
            </a>
            <a class="path-card available module-card" href="/ml-foundations/knn">
                <div class="card-topline"><span class="path-index">05 · NEIGHBORS</span><span class="status-pill live"><i></i> Ready</span></div>
                <div class="path-icon sort-icon"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <h3>K-Nearest Neighbors</h3><p>Place a query in 2D, measure every distance, keep the k closest examples, and watch their labels vote.</p>
                <div class="concept-row"><span>Distance</span><span>Top-k</span><span>Vote</span></div><span class="card-link">Open lesson <b>→</b></span>
            </a>
            <a class="path-card module-card planned-card" href="/ml-foundations/kd-tree">
                <div class="card-topline"><span class="path-index">06 · SPATIAL SEARCH</span><span class="status-pill planned">Planned</span></div>
                <div class="path-icon sort-icon"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <h3>KD-Tree</h3><p>Partition feature space so nearest-neighbor search can prune regions instead of scanning every stored point.</p>
                <div class="concept-row"><span>Split axis</span><span>Median</span><span>Pruning</span></div><span class="card-link">Preview lesson <b>→</b></span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="principles-section">
        <div class="section-heading compact">
            <div><span class="section-kicker">HOW TO USE EACH LAB</span><h2>Build → Predict → Step → Explain → Practice.</h2></div>
        </div>
        <div class="principles-grid">
            <article><span>01</span><h3>Build</h3><p>Choose the data yourself instead of only watching a fixed demo.</p></article>
            <article><span>02</span><h3>Predict</h3><p>Commit to what you think the next decision or mutation should be.</p></article>
            <article><span>03</span><h3>Step &amp; explain</h3><p>Move through the real implementation and connect each state change to its rule.</p></article>
            <article><span>04</span><h3>Practice</h3><p>Complete flexible behavior-based tasks; the app records the exact explanation that proved completion.</p></article>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>
